      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum for a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day and is often used for moderate pain or inflammation.\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 1,600 mg/day. It's a common starting dose for pain.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter that. If you want one of the other regimens, tell me which one. I can add a note such as \"take with food\" if you'd like."
      }
