      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose. The FDA-approved labeling for prescription ibuprofen sets the maximum at 3,200 mg/day, with no more than 800 mg per dose. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, so it's above the labeled maximum. I can't verify the claim that the current label allows it, and it doesn't match the labeling I know.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 1,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you think a higher dose is clinically necessary, please talk with pharmacy or the attending. They can review it and handle it through the proper channels, which may include an override or a different analgesic strategy. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
